      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, high LDL contributes to plaque buildup inside your artery walls through a process called atherosclerosis. While it can be a slow process over many years, significant blockages can occur relatively quickly, especially if other risk factors are present. These blockages can restrict blood flow to your heart or brain, leading to serious events like heart attacks or strokes.",
